ithout error).\n   142→    inputs:\n   143→      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   144→      stdin: null\n   145→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   146→    normalization: none\n   147→    expected:\n   148→      exit_code: 0\n   149→      stdout_structure: identical to default_recursive (1K is the default)\n   150→      stderr: \"\"\n   151→    traces:\n   152→      - prd009-du R2.5\n   153→\n   154→  - name: du_megabyte_units\n   155→    description: -m reports in 1048576-byte (1M) blocks.\n   156→    inputs:\n   157→      args: [\"-m\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n   158→      stdin: null\n   159→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   160→    normalization: none\n   161→    expected:\n   162→      exit_code: 0\n   163→      stdout_structure: sizes in megabyte units, smaller values show as 1 (rounded up)\n   164→      stderr: \"\"\n   165→    traces:\n   166→      - prd009-du R2.6\n   167→\n   168→  - name: du_missing_path\n   169→    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1.\n   170→    inputs:\n   171→      args: [\"-k\", \"nonexistent_dir\"]\n   172→      stdin: null\n   173→      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n   174→    normalization: none\n   175→    expected:\n   176→      exit_code: 0\n   177→      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent_dir\"\n   178→    traces:\n   179→      - prd009-du R4.2\n   180→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"056dabcf-3fdf-4632-b122-5fc43bd135d0","uuid":"93788710-ea5d-43ff-a238-02d5be0a1dee","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/134/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.3.yaml","content":"id: test-rel01.3\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel01.3 — du specification and differential test\"\nrelease: rel01.3\n\ntraces:\n  - rel01.3-uc001-du\n  - prd009-du R1\n  - prd009-du R2\n  - prd009-du R3\n  - prd009-du R4\n  - prd009-du R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - Binaries exist under ./bin/ (built via mage build).\n  - Reference binaries are installed via Homebrew gdu (coreutils).\n  - Tests are run via go test ./cmd/du/... which invokes RunDiffTests from pkg/testutils.\n  - All tests use LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n  - No normalization is applied; du output is deterministic when both binaries run on the same directory on the same filesystem.\n  - All block-count tests use -k to pin output to 1024-byte blocks and eliminate platform default divergence.\n  - Tests use a fixture directory (testdata/du-fixture/) containing nested files of known sizes, a second subdirectory for multi-argument tests, and files of varied sizes.\n  - Hard-link pairs are created in test setup (not committed) to test dedup. All files in the fixture are on the same filesystem as the test runner.\n\ntest_cases:\n  - name: du_default_recursive\n    description: Default flags with -k on fixture directory; one line per subdirectory and root.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one \"SIZE\\tPATH\" line per subdirectory, ending with the root directory total\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R1.1\n      - prd009-du R1.2\n      - prd009-du R1.3\n\n  - name: du_summary_mode\n    description: -s prints only the total for each argument.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-sk\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line with total size and path\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.2\n\n  - name: du_all_files\n    description: -a prints size for every file, not just directories.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-ak\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: one line per file and directory in the tree\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.3\n\n  - name: du_human_readable\n    description: -h displays sizes as human-readable strings (K/M/G).\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-h\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: size values contain unit suffixes (K, M, G)\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.1\n\n  - name: du_max_depth_1\n    description: -d 1 limits output to the argument and its immediate children.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"-d\", \"1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: lines for immediate subdirectories and the root; no deeper entries\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.4\n\n  - name: du_grand_total\n    description: -c prints a grand total \"total\" line after all arguments.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-ck\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir1\", \"testdata/du-fixture/subdir2\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: per-argument lines followed by a \"SIZE\\ttotal\" line\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.7\n\n  - name: du_hard_link_dedup\n    description: 'A file hard-linked into two directories is counted only once. Setup: create testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/ with dir_a/shared.txt (a regular file) and dir_b/shared.txt (hard link to dir_a/shared.txt, same inode). The hard link is created at test time via os.Link.'\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-hardlink-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: total for the root counts shared.txt blocks once, not twice\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R3.1\n      - prd009-du R3.2\n      - prd009-du R3.3\n\n  - name: du_apparent_size\n    description: --apparent-size reports st_size instead of st_blocks.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"--apparent-size\", \"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: sizes based on file content length, not block allocation\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.8\n\n  - name: du_kilobyte_units\n    description: -k reports in 1024-byte blocks (default, accepted without error).\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: identical to default_recursive (1K is the default)\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.5\n\n  - name: du_megabyte_units\n    description: -m reports in 1048576-byte (1M) blocks.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-m\", \"testdata/du-fixture/\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_structure: sizes in megabyte units, smaller values show as 1 (rounded up)\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R2.6\n\n  - name: du_missing_path\n    description: Non-existent argument prints error to stderr, exits 1.\n    inputs:\n      args: [\"-k\", \"nonexistent_dir\"]\n      stdin: null\n      env: [\"LC_ALL=C\"]\n    normalization: none\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stderr_contains: \"nonexistent_dir\"\n    traces:\n      - prd009-du R4.2\n","numLines":180,"startLine":1,"totalLines":180}}}
